# Exa MCP - The Web Search MCP

> Complete setup guide for Exa MCP Server. Connect Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code, and 10+ AI assistants to Exa's web search and code search tools.

Exa MCP connects AI assistants to Exa's search capabilities, including web search and code search. It is open-source and available on GitHub.

<br />

## Installation

<Tabs>
  <Tab title="Cursor">
    ![Install with one click](

    Or add to `~/.cursor/mcp.json`:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "url": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="VS Code">
    ![Install with one click](

    Or add to `.vscode/mcp.json`:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "servers": {
        "exa": {
          "type": "http",
          "url": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Claude Code">
    Run in terminal:

    ```bash  theme={null}
    claude mcp add --transport http exa 
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Claude Desktop">
    Add to your Claude Desktop config file:

    **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`

    **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "command": "npx",
          "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", ""]
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Codex">
    Run in terminal:

    ```bash  theme={null}
    codex mcp add exa --url 
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="OpenCode">
    Add to your `opencode.json`:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcp": {
        "exa": {
          "type": "remote",
          "url": "",
          "enabled": true
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Windsurf">
    Add to `~/.codeium/windsurf/mcp_config.json`:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "serverUrl": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Zed">
    Add to your Zed settings:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "context_servers": {
        "exa": {
          "url": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Gemini CLI">
    Add to `~/.gemini/settings.json`:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "httpUrl": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Google Antigravity">
    Go to the three-dot menu in the Agent panel, navigate to **Manage MCP Servers**, then **View Raw config** and add:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "serverUrl": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="v0 by Vercel">
    In v0, select **Prompt Tools** > **Add MCP** and enter:

    ```

    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Warp">
    Go to **Settings** > **MCP Servers** > **Add MCP Server** and add:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "exa": {
        "url": ""
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Kiro">
    Add to `~/.kiro/settings/mcp.json`:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "url": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Roo Code">
    Add to your Roo Code MCP config:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "type": "streamable-http",
          "url": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Via npm Package">
    Standard `mcpServers` format with the npm package. Get your Exa API key.

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "command": "npx",
          "args": ["-y", "exa-mcp-server"],
          "env": {
            "EXA_API_KEY": "your_api_key"
          }
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>

  <Tab title="Other">
    For other MCP clients that support remote MCP:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "url": ""
        }
      }
    }
    ```

    If your client doesn't support remote MCP servers directly:

    ```json  theme={null}
    {
      "mcpServers": {
        "exa": {
          "command": "npx",
          "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", ""]
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  </Tab>
</Tabs>

## Available Tools

**Enabled by default:**

| Tool                   | Description                                                                                        |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `web_search_exa`       | Search the web for any topic and get clean, ready-to-use content                                   |
| `get_code_context_exa` | Find code examples, documentation, and programming solutions from GitHub, Stack Overflow, and docs |
| `crawling_exa`         | Get the full content of a specific webpage from a known URL                                        |

**Optional** (enable via `tools` parameter):

| Tool                      | Description                                                                             |
| ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `web_search_advanced_exa` | Advanced web search with full control over filters, domains, dates, and content options |

